From db1d4ed6036a2fc07f51c1965151bcd190fe86a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: launch-artifact-cache <agent@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:41:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/256] perf(cpu): add process-level AVX-512 artifact
 semantics cache (launch-artifact-cache)

N4.0 removed the duplicate validation entry points inside one launch, but
_validate_primary_semantics and the body of _decode_artifact still each
reconstructed the same CoreProgram -> Avx512Program lowering and deep-compared
the full vector plan.  On the 6728-op prefill artifact that second pass is
~2 s of lowering + ~0.6 s of plan serialization + comparison.

Add a bounded process-level cache (N4.1) keyed by the immutable artifact
identity: content digest, format/ABI/entrypoint, target digest and the hash of
the deeply-frozen metadata mapping.  A hit additionally requires the exact
frozen metadata object (held strongly) to still be attached to the artifact,
so replacing metadata can never alias an entry, and the verified program
digest / plan digest are pinned in the entry because both are expensive to
recompute (CpuVectorProgram.plan_digest re-serializes every plan per access).

Fail-closed is unchanged and per launch: artifact.validate() + native byte
digest, version triple, declared program/plan/target digests, compile flags,
native safety markers and the host feature contract are all re-checked outside
the cache; a metadata/version/digest/capability mismatch changes the key or
fails one of those checks and is still rejected on every launch.  The per
launch memo now shares its thawed metadata copy, and `_packed_dispatch_for`
accepts the already verified plan digest, so neither rebuilds that work.

Measured on the s3 bracket probe (T=5, 6728 ops, no weights): validate + decode
13.5-15.1 s (lower called twice) -> 5.3 s cold / 0.57 s repeated launch (lower
called once / zero times).  Focused pytest: 96 passed (N4.0 memo 10 cases
included).  The locked interleaved A/B, bit-level and fail-closed evidence
lives in worktrees/_meta/pypto-x/launch-artifact-cache/.
